<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuezhi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yuezhi were a nomadic people who lived in the region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor">Gansu corridor</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in the late first millennium BCE. Defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> in the second century BCE, they migrated westwards to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, where one branch later founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushan-empire">Kushan Empire</a>. Accounts of the Xiongnu Empire discuss their defeat as part of the empire's rise and its wider impact.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuezhi.jpg" alt="Yuezhi" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ALFGRN · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khalchayan_Prince,_side_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
